{"title": "Sectional Mock #78 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The dimensions of a box are 15 m, X m, and 10 m. If the cost of painting the entire box externally is Rs.2898 at Rs.3 per sq. m, then find the volume (in cubic m) of the box.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2366;&#2350; 15 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;, X &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 10 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352;&#2368; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; 3 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 2898 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; (&#2328;&#2344; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1828", "1998", "2108", "1746"], "options_hi": ["1828", "1998", "2108", "1746"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Surface area of the box = Total cost of painting/Rate</p><p>= 2898/3 = 966 sq. m</p><p>So,</p><p>2 * (15X + 10X + 150) = 966</p><p>25X = 483  -  150</p><p>25X = 333</p><p>X= 333/25</p><p>X = 13.32</p><p>Now,</p><p>Volume of the box = 15 * 13.32 * 10</p><p>= 15 * 10 * 1332/100</p><p>= 666 * 3 = 1998 cubic m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Surface area of the box = Total cost of painting/Rate</p><p>= 2898/3 = 966 sq. m</p><p>So,</p><p>2 * (15X + 10X + 150) = 966</p><p>25X = 483  -  150</p><p>25X = 333</p><p>X= 333/25</p><p>X = 13.32</p><p>Now,</p><p>Volume of the box = 15 * 13.32 * 10</p><p>= 15 * 10 * 1332/100</p><p>= 666 * 3 = 1998 cubic m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>On dividing a number by 9, we get 5 as remainder. What will be the remainder when the double of this number is divided by 9?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; 9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["8", "1", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["8", "1", "3", "4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let, the number be 14.</p><p>14/9 =&gt; 5 is remainder</p><p>According to Question,</p><p>(2 * 14)/9 = 28/9 =&gt; 1 is remainder.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the number be 14.</p><p>14/9 =&gt; 5 is remainder</p><p>According to Question,</p><p>(2 * 14)/9 = 28/9 =&gt; 1 is remainder.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If sin&theta; = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>8", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; sin&#952; = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>8", "options_en": ["15/17", "8/15", "15/8", "17/15"], "options_hi": ["15/17", "8/15", "15/8", "17/15"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>sin&#1256; = 8/17</p><p>P = 8, H = 17</p><p>B = &radic; (17<sup>2</sup> - 8<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>B = 15</p><p>tan&#1256; = 8/15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>sin&#1256; = 8/17</p><p>P = 8, H = 17</p><p>B = &radic; (17<sup>2</sup> - 8<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>B = 15</p><p>tan&#1256; = 8/15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>P can win Q by 100 m in a race of 900 m. What should be the change in distance of startup if Q covers 1/3<sup>rd</sup> less distance than that by P in the same time?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>900 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; P, Q &#2360;&#2375; 100 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2368;&#2340; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; Q &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; P &#2360;&#2375; 1/3 &#2325;&#2350; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["400 m", "250 m", "300 m", "200 m"], "options_hi": ["400 &#2350;&#2368;", "250 &#2350;&#2368;", "300 &#2350;&#2368;", "200 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Initially distance covered by P = 900 m</p><p>Distance covered by Q = 900  -  100 = 800 m</p><p>New distance covered by Q = 900 * (1 - 1/3) = 600</p><p>New startup = 800  -  600 = 200 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Initially distance covered by P = 900 m</p><p>Distance covered by Q = 900  -  100 = 800 m</p><p>New distance covered by Q = 900 * (1 - 1/3) = 600</p><p>New startup = 800  -  600 = 200 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average height of three kids is 56 cm and their heights are in the proportion of 7 : 8 : 9. Find the heights of all the three.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2325;&#2342; 56 cm &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2342; 7: 8: 9 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2342; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["42 cm, 48 cm, 54 cm", "56 cm, 64 cm, 72 cm", "35 cm, 40 cm, 45 cm", "49 cm, 56 cm, 63 cm"], "options_hi": ["42 cm, 48 cm, 54 cm", "56 cm, 64 cm, 72 cm", "35 cm, 40 cm, 45 cm", "49 cm, 56 cm, 63 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the heights of three kids is '7x', '8x', and '9x' respectively.</p><p>Average height of all the 3 kids = (7x + 8x + 9x)/3 = 56</p><p>8x = 56</p><p>x = 7</p><p>Height of all the 3 kids is 49 cm, 56 cm, and 63 cm.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the heights of three kids is '7x', '8x', and '9x' respectively.</p><p>Average height of all the 3 kids = (7x + 8x + 9x)/3 = 56</p><p>8x = 56</p><p>x = 7</p><p>Height of all the 3 kids is 49 cm, 56 cm, and 63 cm.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If P =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">x<sup>2</sup> + 4x - 21", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; P = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">x<sup>2</sup> + 4x - 21", "options_en": ["(x+1)/(x+9)", "1", "0", "(x + 7)/(x  -  5)"], "options_hi": ["(x+1)/(x+9)", "1", "0", "(x + 7)/(x - 5)"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=296 height=133 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14931/image005.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=296 height=133 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14931/image005.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper offers 3 schemes of discounts to his customers. Which of the following schemes will fetch the minimum discount percentage?</p><p>I. Two successive discounts of 25% and 32%</p><p>II. Buy 6 get 5 free.</p><p>III. Buy 8 get 7 free.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; 3 &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;?</p><p>I. 25% &#2324;&#2352; 32% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335;</p><p>II. 6 &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>III. 8 &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2306; 7 &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["I", "II", "III", "Both II and III"], "options_hi": ["I", "II", "III", "II &#2324;&#2352; III &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>I. Effective discount = 25 + 32  -  (25 * 32)/100 = 49%</p><p>II. Total items = 11, Paid = 6</p><p>Discount = 5 * 100/11 = 45.45%</p><p>III. Total items = 15, paid = 8 </p><p>Discount = 7 * 100/15 = 46.67% </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>I. Effective discount = 25 + 32  -  (25 * 32)/100 = 49%</p><p>II. Total items = 11, Paid = 6</p><p>Discount = 5 * 100/11 = 45.45%</p><p>III. Total items = 15, paid = 8 </p><p>Discount = 7 * 100/15 = 46.67% </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 9<sup>x</sup> * 27<sup>(1/4) </sup>= 3<sup>(3/4)</sup>, then find the value of x.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 9<sup>x</sup> * 27<sup>(1/4)</sup>= 3<sup>(3/4)</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "3", "0", "2"], "options_hi": ["1", "3", "0", "2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=103 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image029.png\"></p><p><img width=99 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image031.png\"></p><p><img width=53 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image032.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=45 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image035.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=103 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image029.png\"></p><p><img width=99 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image030.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image031.png\"></p><p><img width=53 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image032.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=45 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image035.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The given table shows the expenditure in (in crores &#8377;) of three companies A, B, and C, and the percentage profit of these companies in different years. Given that:</p><p>Income = Expenditure + (Expenditure  X  Profit % / 100)</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Years</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Company A (Expenditure)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Company A (Profit %)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Company B (Expenditure)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Company B (Profit %)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Company C (Expenditure)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Company C (Profit %)</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2002</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">24</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">50%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">45%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2003</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">30</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">45%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">15</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">50</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">55%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2004</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">36</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">65%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2005</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">48%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">80</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">75%</td></tr></table><p>What is the income (in crores &#8377;) of Company C in the year 2003?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; (&#2325;&#2352;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2344; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367;:</p><p>&#2310;&#2351; = &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; + (&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; X &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; % / 100)</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; A (&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; A (&#2354;&#2366;&#2349; %)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; B (&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2368; (&#2354;&#2366;&#2349; %)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2368; (&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2368; (&#2354;&#2366;&#2349; %)</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2002</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">24</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">50%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">45%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2003</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">30</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">45%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">15</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">50</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">55%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2004</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">36</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">25</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">65%</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2005</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">40</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">60%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">35</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">48%</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">80</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">75%</td></tr></table><p>&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 2003 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; (&#2325;&#2352;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["75.7", "77.5", "105", "69.8"], "options_hi": ["75.7", "77.5", "105", "69.8"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Expenditure = &#8377;50 crores</p><p>Profit % = 55%</p><p>=&gt; 50 + (50  X  55)/100 = 50 + 27.5</p><p>Income = &#8377;77.5 crores</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Expenditure = &#8377;50 crores</p><p>Profit % = 55%</p><p>=&gt; 50 + (50  X  55)/100 = 50 + 27.5</p><p>Income = &#8377;77.5 crores</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A certain amount of money becomes thrice in 5 years at compound interest. How many years it will take to become 9 times?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 9 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["15 years", "8 years", "10 years", "25 years"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "8 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "10 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "25 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let principal = P</p><p>Amount = 3P</p><p>P(1 + r/100)<sup>5</sup> = 3P</p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>5</sup> = 3</p><p>For 9 times: </p><p>P(1 + r/100)<sup>t</sup> = 9P, </p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>t</sup> = 9 = 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>t</sup> = (1 + r/100)<sup>5*2</sup></p><p>t = 10 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let principal = P</p><p>Amount = 3P</p><p>P(1 + r/100)<sup>5</sup> = 3P</p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>5</sup> = 3</p><p>For 9 times: </p><p>P(1 + r/100)<sup>t</sup> = 9P, </p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>t</sup> = 9 = 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>(1 + r/100)<sup>t</sup> = (1 + r/100)<sup>5*2</sup></p><p>t = 10 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the sides of a triangle are 36 cm, 42 cm, and 50 cm, respectively, then find the area of the triangle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 42 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["214&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup>", "224&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup>", "216&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup>", "208&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["214&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "224&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "216&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "208&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The sides of a triangle are 36 cm, 42 cm, and 50 cm, respectively.</p><p>S = (16 + 42 + 70)/2 = 64 cm</p><p>Hence, area = &radic;[s(s  -  a)(s  -  b)(s  -  c)] = &radic;[64 * 28 * 22 * 14] = 224&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The sides of a triangle are 36 cm, 42 cm, and 50 cm, respectively.</p><p>S = (16 + 42 + 70)/2 = 64 cm</p><p>Hence, area = &radic;[s(s  -  a)(s  -  b)(s  -  c)] = &radic;[64 * 28 * 22 * 14] = 224&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The volumes of two spheres are in the ratio of 512: 3375. The ratio of their surface areas is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 512: 3375 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["64:225", "49:325", "27:144", "68:125"], "options_hi": ["64:225", "49:325", "27:144", "68:125"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of volumes of two spheres = 512:3375</p><p>(4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/3)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup>/3) = 512/3375</p><p>r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup> = (8/15)<sup>3</sup></p><p>r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub> = 8/15</p><p>Ratio of their surface areas = (4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>= (8/15)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 64/225</p><p>= 64:225</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of volumes of two spheres = 512:3375</p><p>(4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/3)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup>/3) = 512/3375</p><p>r<sub>1</sub><sup>3</sup>/r<sub>2</sub><sup>3</sup> = (8/15)<sup>3</sup></p><p>r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub> = 8/15</p><p>Ratio of their surface areas = (4&#960;r<sub>1</sub><sup>2</sup>)/(4&#960;r<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup>) </p><p>= (r<sub>1</sub>/r<sub>2</sub>)<sup>2</sup> </p><p>= (8/15)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 64/225</p><p>= 64:225</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The value of the expression &radic;7  - &radic;(12 - 2&radic;35) is closest to:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &radic;7 - &radic;(12 - 2&radic;35) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["4.0", "2.2", "2.8", "3.0"], "options_hi": ["4.0", "2.2", "2.8", "3.0"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=112 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image098.gif\"></p><p><img width=249 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image099.gif\"></p><p><img width=127 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image100.gif\"></p><p><img width=100 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image101.gif\"></p><p><img width=35 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image102.gif\"></p><p><img width=44 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image103.gif\"></p><p>The value is close to 2.2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=112 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image098.gif\"></p><p><img width=249 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image099.gif\"></p><p><img width=127 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image100.gif\"></p><p><img width=100 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image101.gif\"></p><p><img width=35 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image102.gif\"></p><p><img width=44 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image103.gif\"></p><p>The value is close to 2.2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the area of a triangle whose altitude and base are 17 cm and 10 cm, respectively.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["102 sq. cm", "68 sq. cm", "85 sq. cm", "91 sq. cm"], "options_hi": ["102 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "68 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "85 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "91 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Area of triangle = (1/2) x base x altitude</p><p>= (1/2) x 10 x 17</p><p>= 85 sq. cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of triangle = (1/2) x base x altitude</p><p>= (1/2) x 10 x 17</p><p>= 85 sq. cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following pie chart shows the percentage distribution of number of people who likes different beverages. Total number of people who likes different beverages are 2700. Study the graph carefully and answer the question that follows.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20812/image022.png\"></p><p>P: Average number of people who likes Tea, Coffee and Fruit juice.</p><p>Q: Average number of people who likes Iced tea, Milkshake and Cold coffee.</p><p>Find the value of (3Q  -  2P).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2375;&#2351; &#2346;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2375;&#2351; &#2346;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 2700 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20812/image022.png\"></p><p>P: &#2330;&#2366;&#2351;, &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2370;&#2335; &#2332;&#2370;&#2360; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p>Q: &#2310;&#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2337; &#2335;&#2368;, &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2358;&#2375;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2377;&#2347;&#2368; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404;</p><p>(3Q - 2P) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["190", "219", "228", "189"], "options_hi": ["190", "219", "228", "189"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><b>P:</b> Total number of people who likes Tea, Coffee and Fruit juice = 2700 * (20+10+12)% = 1134</p><p>Average number of people who likes Tea, Coffee and Fruit juice = 1134/3 = 378</p><p><b>Q:</b> Total number of people who likes Iced tea, Milkshake and Cold coffee = 2700 * (11+8+16)% = 945</p><p>Average number of people who likes Iced tea, Milkshake and Cold coffee = 945/3 = 315</p><p>3Q  -  2P = 3*315  -  2*378 = 945  -  756 = 189</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>P:</b> Total number of people who likes Tea, Coffee and Fruit juice = 2700 * (20+10+12)% = 1134</p><p>Average number of people who likes Tea, Coffee and Fruit juice = 1134/3 = 378</p><p><b>Q:</b> Total number of people who likes Iced tea, Milkshake and Cold coffee = 2700 * (11+8+16)% = 945</p><p>Average number of people who likes Iced tea, Milkshake and Cold coffee = 945/3 = 315</p><p>3Q  -  2P = 3*315  -  2*378 = 945  -  756 = 189</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If &radic;(5 * p) * &radic;5 = &radic;1584  -  &radic;396  -  &radic;275 + &radic;176, then what is the value of 'p'?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &radic;(5 * p) * &radic;5 = &radic;1584 - &radic;396 - &radic;275 + &radic;176, &#2340;&#2379; 'p' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; ?</p>", "options_en": ["7", "11", "13", "17"], "options_hi": ["7", "11", "13", "17"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>=> &radic;(5 * p) * &radic;5 = &radic;1584  -  &radic;396  -  &radic;275 + &radic;176</p><p>=> (&radic;5 * &radic;5) * &radic;p = &radic;(144 * 11)  -  &radic;(36 * 11)  -  &radic;(25 * 11) + &radic;(16 * 11)</p><p>=> 5&radic;p = 12&radic;11  -  6&radic;11  -  5&radic;11 + 4&radic;11</p><p>=> 5&radic;p = 5&radic;11</p><p>=> p = 11</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>=> &radic;(5 * p) * &radic;5 = &radic;1584  -  &radic;396  -  &radic;275 + &radic;176</p><p>=> (&radic;5 * &radic;5) * &radic;p = &radic;(144 * 11)  -  &radic;(36 * 11)  -  &radic;(25 * 11) + &radic;(16 * 11)</p><p>=> 5&radic;p = 12&radic;11  -  6&radic;11  -  5&radic;11 + 4&radic;11</p><p>=> 5&radic;p = 5&radic;11</p><p>=> p = 11</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train running at the speed of 126 km/h crosses a platform in 60 seconds. If the length of the train is double, then the same train crosses the platform in 80 seconds. Find the length of the train. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>126 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 80 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["700 m", "1400 m", "1000 m", "900 m"], "options_hi": ["700 &#2350;&#2368;", "1400 &#2350;&#2368;", "1000 &#2350;&#2368;", "900 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of the train = 126 * 5/18 = 35 m/sec [To convert km/h into m/sec multiply by 5/18] </p><p>Distance = Speed * Time</p><p>Let the length of the train and platform be x m and y m respectively. </p><p>x + y = 35 * 60 ... (i)</p><p>2x + y = 35 * 80 ... (ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii) </p><p>x = 700 m</p><p>y = 1400 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of the train = 126 * 5/18 = 35 m/sec [To convert km/h into m/sec multiply by 5/18] </p><p>Distance = Speed * Time</p><p>Let the length of the train and platform be x m and y m respectively. </p><p>x + y = 35 * 60 ... (i)</p><p>2x + y = 35 * 80 ... (ii)</p><p>From (i) and (ii) </p><p>x = 700 m</p><p>y = 1400 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 2A : 8 &#8759; X : (A/3), then X = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 2A : 8 &#8759; X : (A/3) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X = ?</p>", "options_en": ["A/6", "2A/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/12"], "options_hi": ["A/6", "2A/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/12"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>2A * (A/3) =8 * X</p><p>X = (2A<sup>2</sup>/3) * 1/8</p><p>X = A<sup>2</sup>/12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>2A * (A/3) =8 * X</p><p>X = (2A<sup>2</sup>/3) * 1/8</p><p>X = A<sup>2</sup>/12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a right  -  angled triangle XYZ, &#8736;Y = 90&deg; and &#8736;X and &#8736;Z are acute angles. If cosecX = 5&radic;2, then find the value of sinZcosY + cosXsinY.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; XYZ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;Y = 90&deg; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#8736;X &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;Z &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cosecX = 5&radic;2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; sinZcosY + cosXsinY &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7&radic;2/10", "5&radic;2/7", "49/10", "4&radic;2/5"], "options_hi": ["7&radic;2/10", "5&radic;2/7", "49/10", "4&radic;2/5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=281 height=225 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26460/image024.png\"></p><p>cosecX = 5&radic;2</p><p>H/P = 5&radic;2/1</p><p>B = &radic;[(5&radic;2)<sup>2</sup>  -  1<sup>2</sup>] = 7</p><p>sinZcosY + cosXsinY</p><p>= (7/5&radic;2) * cos90&deg; + (7/5&radic;2) * sin90&deg;</p><p>= 0 + (7/5&radic;2)</p><p>= 7&radic;2/10</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=281 height=225 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26460/image024.png\"></p><p>cosecX = 5&radic;2</p><p>H/P = 5&radic;2/1</p><p>B = &radic;[(5&radic;2)<sup>2</sup>  -  1<sup>2</sup>] = 7</p><p>sinZcosY + cosXsinY</p><p>= (7/5&radic;2) * cos90&deg; + (7/5&radic;2) * sin90&deg;</p><p>= 0 + (7/5&radic;2)</p><p>= 7&radic;2/10</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a and b are roots of quadratic equation x<sup>2</sup>  -  22x + 85 = 0 and a &gt; b, then how many numbers between 100 and 1500 are divisible by both (a  -  b) and average of a and b?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a &#2324;&#2352; b &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; x<sup>2</sup> - 22x + 85 = 0 &#2324;&#2352; a &gt; b &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; 100 &#2324;&#2352; 1500 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; (a - b) &#2324;&#2352; a &#2324;&#2352; b &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["9", "11", "15", "17"], "options_hi": ["9", "11", "15", "17"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  22x + 85 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  17x  -  5x + 85 = 0</p><p>x = 17, 5</p><p>a = 17, b = 5</p><p>a  -  b = 17  -  5 = 12</p><p>Average of a and b = (17 + 5)/2 = 11</p><p>Numbers divisible by both 12 and 11 = numbers divisible by LCM of 12 and 11</p><p>LCM of 12 and 11 = 132</p><p>Numbers between 100 and 1500 which are divisible by 132 = 132, 264,...., 1452.</p><p>Total numbers = ((1452  -  132)/1320 + 1 = 11</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  22x + 85 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  17x  -  5x + 85 = 0</p><p>x = 17, 5</p><p>a = 17, b = 5</p><p>a  -  b = 17  -  5 = 12</p><p>Average of a and b = (17 + 5)/2 = 11</p><p>Numbers divisible by both 12 and 11 = numbers divisible by LCM of 12 and 11</p><p>LCM of 12 and 11 = 132</p><p>Numbers between 100 and 1500 which are divisible by 132 = 132, 264,...., 1452.</p><p>Total numbers = ((1452  -  132)/1320 + 1 = 11</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A certain sum of money is given at a certain rate of simple interest for 6 years. Had it been given at 7% higher rate, it would have fetched &#8377;1,512 more. Find the sum (in &#8377;).</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 6 &#8203;&#8203;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 7% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; 1,512 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2404; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; (&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["3200", "3600", "3100", "4200"], "options_hi": ["3200", "3600", "3100", "4200"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the sum be P.</p><p>SI for increased rate = &#8377;1,512</p><p>Increased rate = (Rate + 7)%</p><p>Difference in SI = (P  X  7  X  6) / 100</p><p>=&gt; &#8377;1,512 = (P  X  42) / 100</p><p>=&gt; 1512 = 0.42P</p><p>=&gt; P = 1512 / 0.42</p><p>=&gt; P = 3600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the sum be P.</p><p>SI for increased rate = &#8377;1,512</p><p>Increased rate = (Rate + 7)%</p><p>Difference in SI = (P  X  7  X  6) / 100</p><p>=&gt; &#8377;1,512 = (P  X  42) / 100</p><p>=&gt; 1512 = 0.42P</p><p>=&gt; P = 1512 / 0.42</p><p>=&gt; P = 3600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B and C share profit equally. C is guaranteed 10% on his investment of &#8377;50000. If total profit is &#8377;9000, how much extra must C receive?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352;-&#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; C &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; 50000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2346;&#2352; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 9000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; C &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 2000", "Rs. 2500", "Rs. 1800", "Rs. 3000"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 2000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2500", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1800", "&#2352;&#2369;. 3000"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Guaranteed = 10% of 50000 = Rs. 5000</p><p>Actual equal share = 1/3  X  9000 = Rs. 3000</p><p>Deficiency = 5000  -  3000 = Rs. 2000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Guaranteed = 10% of 50000 = Rs. 5000</p><p>Actual equal share = 1/3  X  9000 = Rs. 3000</p><p>Deficiency = 5000  -  3000 = Rs. 2000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>When 27 is added to a two digit number, its digits get reversed. What is the difference between its units digit and tens digit?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 27 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2313;&#2354;&#2335; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "3", "4", "5"], "options_hi": ["2", "3", "4", "5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the two digit number be 'ab' = 10a + b</p><p>Given that,</p><p>10a + b + 27 = 10b + a</p><p>=&gt; 27 = 9*(b-a)</p><p>=&gt;b-a = 3</p><p>Hence the difference would be 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the two digit number be 'ab' = 10a + b</p><p>Given that,</p><p>10a + b + 27 = 10b + a</p><p>=&gt; 27 = 9*(b-a)</p><p>=&gt;b-a = 3</p><p>Hence the difference would be 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The given pie-chart shows the percentage distribution of the expenditure incurred in publishing a book.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27249/image025.png\"></p><p>What is the central angle of the sector corresponding to the expenditure incurred on binding?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312;-&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 4\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27249/image025.png\"></p><p>&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["78.8&deg;", "61.8&deg;", "82.8&deg;", "48.8&deg;"], "options_hi": ["78.8&deg;", "61.8&deg;", "82.8&deg;", "48.8&deg;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The percentage of expenditure incurred on binding =23%</p><p>So , central angle = 23*360/100=82.8&deg; .</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The percentage of expenditure incurred on binding =23%</p><p>So , central angle = 23*360/100=82.8&deg; .</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The speeds of A and B are in the ratio 3 : 5. A takes 30 minutes more than B to reach the destination. In how much time does A reach the destination?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 3:5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2379; &#2327;&#2306;&#2340;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2305;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; B &#2360;&#2375; 30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; A &#2327;&#2306;&#2340;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2305;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1 hour 15 minutes", "1 hour 10 minutes", "1 hour", "1 hour 5 minutes"], "options_hi": ["1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; 15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; 10 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; 5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of A and B is '3x' and '5x' respectively.</p><p>Let the time taken by A and B to reach the destination is 't' hours and 't  -  0.5' hours respectively.</p><p>Total distance = 3x * t = 5x * (t  -  0.5)</p><p>3t = 5t  -  2.5</p><p>2t = 2.5</p><p>t = 1.25 hours = 1 hour 15 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of A and B is '3x' and '5x' respectively.</p><p>Let the time taken by A and B to reach the destination is 't' hours and 't  -  0.5' hours respectively.</p><p>Total distance = 3x * t = 5x * (t  -  0.5)</p><p>3t = 5t  -  2.5</p><p>2t = 2.5</p><p>t = 1.25 hours = 1 hour 15 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}]}